Kept the content styles of `@plone/plate` off Volto's own elements that share Plate's class names: the text editor of Volto's text blocks (`slate-editor`) and the view of its table block (`slate-table`). Their `overflow: hidden` hid the slash menu of Volto's text blocks and stopped them from wrapping around floated images in the editor, and the table block got extra padding. @sneridagh
